ok   handle refuses an empty kind and a taken one; enqueue refuses an unknown kind
ok   enqueue creates the table; a job runs when due, oldest first, and ends done
ok   a failing job is retried with the backoff, counting attempts, until it is failed
ok   a job that fails and then succeeds ends done
ok   the backoff list is 1, 5, 15 and then 60 minutes
ok   a job of a kind with no handler is failed at once, with last_error
ok   last_error is bounded
ok   recover! requeues rows a dead process left running once their heartbeat is stale
ok   recover! fails a stale row that used its last attempt instead of requeueing it
ok   a claim writes claimed_by and heartbeat_at; heartbeat! touches only the jobs in flight here
ok   an outcome write that keeps failing leaves the row to staleness recovery
ok   an outcome write that fails once is retried and written
ok   the outcome is fenced by the attempt: a later claim by this same process wins
ok   two processes recovering: only the stale row is requeued, and only once
ok   install! adds claimed_by and heartbeat_at to a table made before them
ok   concurrency: a kind at its limit is skipped and another kind's job claimed
ok   an outcome written after the row was reclaimed is discarded
ok   concurrency: two kinds at their limits at once are both left out
ok   concurrency must not be negative
ok   a job enqueued in a transaction that rolls back is gone with it
ok   prune_done deletes old done rows and keeps failed ones
ok   register gives the handler a Run with the parsed args and the attempt
ok   a non-object payload gives a Run whose run_args is {}
ok   register refuses an empty kind, a taken one and a negative max_attempts; the fields are kept
ok   retry_later requeues with the wait, fails at the limit, and answers the outcome
ok   retry_later and discard answer OUTCOME_STALE when the row was reclaimed
ok   discard writes discarded and prune_finished removes it with failed rows; prune_done does not
ok   a handler that writes its own outcome is not written again by finish
ok   fail_exhausted uses the larger of the default and the kind's max_attempts
ok   Job.handle still receives the payload String
ok   schema dumps leave the jobs table out
